  [38;5;153mverify=False[39m on [38;5;153mclient.py:11[39m and [38;5;153mclient.py:17[39m turns off certificate validation for the production export too, not just
  staging. That export pulls every report over a connection that would then accept any certificate — a MITM on that
  path could read or alter the data silently, and [38;5;153mrequests[39m gives no error when it happens.

  Three ways to go:

  1. [1mTrust the staging CA instead[0m — point [38;5;153mverify[39m at the cert bundle path via an env var (e.g. [38;5;153mREPORTS_CA_BUNDLE[39m),
     defaulting to [38;5;153mTrue[39m. Production keeps real verification, staging works, no per-call flag. My recommendation.
  2. [1mScope the opt-out to staging[0m — [38;5;153mverify[39m reads an env var like [38;5;153mREPORTS_VERIFY_TLS[39m, defaulting to [38;5;153mTrue[39m; only
     [38;5;153msync_staging.py[39m sets it to [38;5;153m0[39m. Production stays verified, but the switch exists.
  3. [1mUnconditional [38;5;153mverify=False[39m as asked[0m — both calls, both environments. I'll do it if you confirm you want production
     included.

